%I A113223 #15 Oct 06 2026 11:05:58
%S A113223 7,5,0,3,7,2,0,3,6,6,0,5,1
%N A113223 Decimal expansion of Integral_{t=0..1} F(t)^F(t) dt, where F(t) is the Cantor function.
%C A113223 The constant lies between 0.750372036605173308402918 and 0.750372036605196407001110, certifying the first 13 decimal digits. - _Eric W. Weisstein_, Oct 06 2026
%H A113223 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/CantorFunction.html">Cantor Function</a>.
%F A113223 The constant equals Sum_{m>=1} 3^(-m)*Sum_{j=1..2^(m-1)} ((2*j-1)/2^m)^((2*j-1)/2^m). - _Eric W. Weisstein_, Oct 06 2026
%e A113223 0.7503720366051... - _Eric W. Weisstein_, Oct 06 2026
%t A113223 With[{s = Table[With[{x = N[Range[1, 2^m - 1, 2]/2^m, 50]}, Total[x^x]/3^m], {m, 18}]}, IntegerDigits[Floor[10^13 (Total[s] + 2 Last[s])]]] (* _Eric W. Weisstein_, Oct 06 2026 *)
%Y A113223 Cf. A095844, A095845.
%K A113223 nonn,cons,more,changed
